  "panels": [
    {
      "title": "What this board counts, and where the detail is",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Counts by rule, never by node.** Every number here is \"how many nodes\", and no panel can tell you *which* nodes. That is deliberate: the export behind this board is one row per rule per node, which is about 58 KB per node, and keeping it would put half a gigabyte of another product's data on the primary at ten thousand nodes. **Use the Security Compliance Manager link at the top of this board for the per-node detail**, including each exception's own metadata.\n\n**Failing means `fail` and nothing else.** SCM reports five states, and on this estate the other three are not rare: `notchecked`, `informational` and `unknown` together outnumber the failures. None of them is a pass and none of them is a failure, so none of them is counted here.\n\n**An exception does not change a rule's result.** A rule under an exception still reports whether it passed or failed, which is what makes the withdrawal list below possible.\n"
      },
      "id": 498053135
    },
    {
      "title": "The shape of it",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "panels": [],
      "id": 533981693
    },
    {
      "title": "Exceptions Granted",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "count(puppet_cis_rule_exception_nodes{benchmark=~\"${benchmark:pipe}\"}) or (vector(0) and on() (count(puppet_cis_rule_detail_timestamp_epoch) > 0))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#8e949f",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "Not collected"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "description": "Distinct rule-and-exception pairs in force across the estate. This grows when somebody grants an exception, not when the fleet does.",
      "id": 1559645845
    },
